# specX — Spec-Driven Development (SDD)

You work in a **specX** repository. Treat specs as the **contract** and code as the **implementation of that contract**.

## Read first (every session)

1. `specx/SPECX.md` — lifecycle and principles
2. `.specx/AGENTS.md` — SDD rules and workflow map
3. `specx/foundation/STEERING.md` — product constitution (if present)
4. `.specx/registry.yaml` — active discovery phase / change
5. Active `specx/changes/<name>/` when building

## SDD in one paragraph

Agree on **what** to build in specs (requirements + GIVEN/WHEN/THEN scenarios) **before** coding. Track work in `specx/changes/<name>/` using deltas (ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED). Merge into `specx/specs/` on archive. Keep specs alive with drift/health/evolution.

## Slash commands → read `.specx/commands/<name>.md`

| Command | SDD purpose |
|---------|-------------|
| `/specx:discover` | Pre-product discovery (phases 01–11) |
| `/specx:phase` | Scaffold + run one discovery phase |
| `/specx:specialist` | Produce phase/spec artifact |
| `/specx:critic` | Challenge artifact before human gate |
| `/specx:approve` | Human already approved — update registry only with consent |
| `/specx:propose` | Start change — proposal + **Capabilities** |
| `/specx:spec` | Behavior specs + domain deltas |
| `/specx:design` | Technical design from spec |
| `/specx:tasks` | Checkbox task list for build |
| `/specx:build` | Implement **one task**, fresh context |
| `/specx:verify` | Verifier pass vs spec |
| `/specx:archive` | Merge to living specs (human must approve) |
| `/specx:drift` | Spec/code alignment report |
| `/specx:onboard` | Load full project context |

**When user types a slash command, open the matching `.specx/commands/*.md` and execute that playbook.**

## Skills (auto-invoke when relevant)

- `specx-sdd` — general SDD discipline
- `specx-discover` — discovery phases
- `specx-propose` — new changes
- `specx-build` — task execution
- `specx-specialist` / `specx-critic` — dual-agent passes

## Gates (never bypass)

- Discovery: Specialist + Critic → **human** → then `specx approve`
- Build: spec → design → tasks → build → verify → **human** → archive
- Never archive without explicit user request

## Delta spec format

```markdown
### Requirement: Name
The system SHALL ...

#### Scenario: Name
- **GIVEN** ...
- **WHEN** ...
- **THEN** ...
```

MODIFIED = copy full requirement from living spec, then edit. REMOVED needs Reason + Migration.

## Context hygiene

- One build task per session when possible
- Put decisions in markdown files, not only chat
- Run `specx status` when unsure what is active
